          "strict": true,
          "description": "Edit a text file inside the workroot synchronously. Supply path, old_text and new_text as exact strings. Existing files require a successful inspect-file followed by read-file of the unchanged content, both fully visible. Literal old_text must start at a physical line boundary including indentation and occur exactly once globally; new_text replaces that occurrence, and may be longer or empty. Use @ex_meckh_line[N] as the entire old_text to insert before physical line N (1..L+1, L+1 appends); include your own newlines. Use @ex_meckh_all to rewrite the whole file. To DELETE an existing file, use old_text=\"@ex_meckh_all\" and new_text=\"@ex_meckh_delete\". Each marker must start with @ immediately, with no leading or trailing space or newline, including native parameter framing newlines. Empty new_text removes content but keeps the file. To create a missing file use all or line[1], including empty new_text, without inspect/read; its parent must already exist. The @ex_meckh_ family is reserved even inside ordinary text. No implicit escaping, normalization or truncation. The server pauses after path for authorization; missing/stale inspection triggers automatic inspection, while a missing read requires a new explicit read. Changed files and invalid paths/markers/selections are rejected without writes."
        }
